[{:db/id "q-347457/field-1/c16bf8c335149e414500b3c2d2f63e44034f5838f47751c2b99b13941fe30b19" :answer/id #uuid "15895814-bf2e-5004-853d-87009382216a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+2x+2x^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347457/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c056a337-6b9c-5ce3-8f58-d027e15d3996" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347457/field-1/c16bf8c335149e414500b3c2d2f63e44034f5838f47751c2b99b13941fe30b19" :answer-field/choices ["q-347457/field-1/c16bf8c335149e414500b3c2d2f63e44034f5838f47751c2b99b13941fe30b19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347457" :question/id #uuid "142d72c5-f07c-59e3-8624-327c5b5bc9ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-347457" :question/problem "Find the second-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{2}(x)$ of $f(x)={e}^{2x}$ about $x=0.$\n\n${P}_{2}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the second-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n{P}_{2}(x)=f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)(x-0)+\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(0)(x-0)^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to work out $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ and ${f}^{″}(0):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{2x} & ⟹ &  & f(0) & =1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =2{e}^{2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =4{e}^{2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ and ${f}^{″}(0)$ into our second-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{2}(x) & =1+2x+\\frac{4}{2}{x}^{2} \\\\  & =1+2x+2{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-347457/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33159d0b-24b5-587e-89e1-b545c2be59c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347457"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8214/selection/4f3582ff880630e3f0a018ef80945e2737a54632834afc62cf3152052062f805" :answer/id #uuid "65229be1-45d9-5049-